          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every Arbonne shake is low in sugar</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Simply1 has under 1 g of sugar per serving, but the original FeelFit and older Essentials mixes used cane sugar, with reviewers reporting about 7 g a serving. Two shakes a day doubles that. Check which version you are buying and read the nutrition panel, rather than trusting the green packaging or the word clean.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating B Corp status as product testing</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Arbonne's B Corp certification grades company practices such as sourcing, energy and employee policies. It does not test the powder for lead, cadmium or banned substances. If contaminant testing matters to you, look for NSF Certified for Sport, Informed Sport or published certificates of analysis, which Arbonne does not provide for its shakes.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying from unknown resellers</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Arbonne now sells its own shakes on Amazon, so there is little reason to buy from a marketplace reseller or an import site. Third-party stock can be old, heat-damaged, a regional formula or an outdated version. Check that the seller is Arbonne International, LLC, and look at the best-by date the day the bag arrives.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Doubling up on vitamins</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Each FeelFit serving carries a full vitamin and mineral blend, which is why Arbonne caps intake at two shakes a day. Adding a separate multivitamin, or a second fortified shake, can push some nutrients well above what you need. If you take medication or supplements already, ask a pharmacist or doctor before stacking them.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing price per bag instead of per gram</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A $101 bag sounds like other premium powders until you divide by the protein. At 20 g a serving, Simply1 works out to about $4.21 per 25 g of protein, against $1.35 to $1.90 for the Amazon alternatives here. Always compare cost per 25 g, because serving sizes and protein doses vary widely.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
